## When the captain stops for a word with someone.
const TALK := {
	"miller": ["Can't complain, sir. Well, I can. I'm choosing not to.", "The crew's steady. Maya's sharper every watch. Don't tell her I said so.", "My wife thinks I'm on a training cruise. In a way, I suppose I am.", "Get some rest when you can, Captain. That's not advice, it's a professional observation."],
	"basse": ["You want food or you want to talk? Food is better. Talking is free, though.", "My father sailed the Kiel canal for forty years. He'd have hated this boat. Too small to walk around in a temper.", "Liquorice? No. That is for emergencies. And for poker.", "The young ones don't eat enough. I watch. Somebody has to."],
	"freja": ["It's the low frequencies I like. You feel them before you hear them.", "My grandmother lived on Gotland. Lighthouse family. I think that's where I learned to watch the dark.", "I'm fine, Captain. Tired, but fine. Mostly fine.", "When it's quiet like this I can hear our own pumps breathing."],
	"erik": ["Ask me about the boat, I'll talk all day. Ask me about me, I go back to the boat.", "Two kids in Tromsø. They think I fix submarines. Mostly I fix Basse's oven.", "She's a good boat, Captain. Treat her gently and she'll bring us home.", "Don't push her past fourteen knots unless you mean it. She'll do it, but she'll remember."],
	"maya": ["Navigation's on track, Captain. I'll keep it that way.", "One day I'd like my own boat. Not yet. Soon, maybe.", "My brother's a fisherman out of Lunenburg. He'd laugh at how slowly we go.", "Can I ask you something, Captain? How do you decide when you don't have enough information? ...Never mind. I think I know."],
}
